{title: Rock of Ages, Cleft for Me}
{artist: Augustus M. Toplady (1740-1778)}
{key: Bb}
{copyright: Public Domain}

{sov: Verse 1}
[Bb]Rock of Ages, [Eb]cleft for [Bb]me,
[F]Let me hide my[Bb]self in Thee;
[F]Let the water [Bb]and the blood,
[F]From Thy wounded [Bb]side which flowed,
[Bb]Be of sin the [Eb]double [Bb]cure,
[F]Save from wrath and [Bb]make me pure.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 2}
[Bb]Not the labors [Eb]of my [Bb]hands
[F]Can fulfill Thy [Bb]law’s demands;
[F]Could my zeal no [Bb]respite know,
[F]Could my tears for[Bb]ever flow,
[Bb]All for sin could [Eb]not a[Bb]tone;
[F]Thou must save, and [Bb]Thou alone.
{eov}

{sov: Verse 3}
[Bb]Nothing in my [Eb]hand I [Bb]bring,
[F]Simply to the [Bb]cross I cling;
[F]Naked, come to [Bb]Thee for dress;
[F]Helpless, look to [Bb]Thee for grace;
[Bb]Foul, I to the [Eb]fountain [Bb]fly;
[F]Wash me, Savior, [Bb]or I die.
{eov}
